<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I63b3be8ee1254890f46a35b7306a35f059ac330d" commit="e88ff3d21d0f4878a427858477e3c9fa31e4282c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: phy: rockchip-dp: should be a child device of the GRF  The displayport-phy is fully enclosed in the general register files (GRF). Therefore as seen from the device-tree it shouldn't be a separate platform- device but instead a sub-device of the GRF - using the simply-mfd mechanism.  The driver entered the kernel in the current merge-window, so we can still adapt the binding without needing a fallback, as the binding hasn't been released with a full kernel yet.  While the edp phy is fully part of the GRF, it doesn't have any separate register set there, so doesn't get any register-area assigned.  Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; Acked-by: Rob Herring &lt;robh@kernel.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kishon Vijay Abraham I &lt;kishon@ti.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 0311c76e4722b8d6e5fa47eaee63c6552bcc74f5)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52691 TEST=Build and boot rk3399  Change-Id: I63b3be8ee1254890f46a35b7306a35f059ac330d Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341320 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="341320" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/341320/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I3a799e7177913fe77f6ee968c6e5ea61df866912" commit="d3b549503af55dae16e85fb1dbf9b8df33a4329f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: phy: rockchip-emmc: should be a child device of the GRF  The emmc-phy is fully enclosed in the general register files (GRF). Therefore as seen from the device-tree it shouldn't be a separate platform- device but instead a sub-device of the GRF - using the simply-mfd mechanism.  The driver entered the kernel in the current merge-window, so we can still adapt the binding without needing a fallback, as the binding hasn't been released with a full kernel yet.  Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; Acked-by: Rob Herring &lt;robh@kernel.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn Lin &lt;shawn.lin@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kishon Vijay Abraham I &lt;kishon@ti.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 332184adff50de9596f03735496c545e8bccc73e)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52691 TEST=Build and boot; test eMMC (with custom eMMC nodes added to DTS)  Change-Id: I3a799e7177913fe77f6ee968c6e5ea61df866912 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341321 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="341321" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/341321/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Iaac46cdb6fad17f88994e5aed3d387816f2e2a19" commit="db10faee33417f7271476a9ed95557198c17386d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: phy: rockchip-emmc: adapt binding to specifiy register offset and length  The emmc-phy occupies a contiguous set of 8 registers inside the general register files, so the reg property should specify this.  Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; Acked-by: Rob Herring &lt;robh@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Kishon Vijay Abraham I &lt;kishon@ti.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5128de85124c728cdbb6b35bd9dc7410f02c0ca1)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52691 TEST=Build and boot; test eMMC (with custom eMMC DT nodes)  Change-Id: Iaac46cdb6fad17f88994e5aed3d387816f2e2a19 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt